# The Village of Barovia's few people out by day (lane 4, F2): Goodwife Petra carrying water from the well. She walks
# her route (the location's `path`) and is indoors long before dark. Lane 28 (2026-10-08) added Grigore hauling his
# firewood in from the west road and Widow Ileana at her husband's grave. NPC depth, batch 1 (docs/plans/
# npc_depth_and_quests.md; lines drafted by Gemini, edited): Vasile and Petre have nothing new to say, and one wrong
# rumour; Petre's coat; Anca learns her name; the goat turns up in the shop, the church and at the Death House gate.

~ goodwife
if flag.bride_buried
Goodwife Petra [smile]: My brother filled in a grave this week and dug no new one. First time in forty years. He doesn't know what to do with his hands. I've given him my garden.
-> END
endif
if flag.burgomaster_buried
Goodwife Petra: They say the old burgomaster's in the ground at last. Good. A man shouldn't lie in his own parlour waiting for the priest.
-> goodwife_menu
endif
Goodwife Petra [afraid]: Strangers. Don't stand so close to the well. Folk will think you've come to poison it, and then they'll think it's my fault for talking to you.
-> goodwife_menu

~ goodwife_menu
* [if quest.six_feet and not flag.bride_story_known] Your brother Mihail is worried about you. -> village_of_barovia/six_feet:petra
* [if not flag.burgomaster_buried] Who would poison a well? -> poison
* [if not quest.the_goatherds_count] Whose goats are those, up on the hill? -> village_of_barovia/the_goatherds_count:petra
* [if flag.vasile_wrong_heard] Vasile says the burgomaster's dog has learned to talk. -> petra_correction
* [if quest.the_fourth_rumour == planted and not flag.fourth_rumour_echoed] Heard anything lately? -> village_of_barovia/the_fourth_rumour:petra_echo
* We'll leave you be. -> END

~ petra_correction
Goodwife Petra [weary]: Vasile told you the hound speaks? Last winter Vasile told the whole lane my well was haunted by a drowned choir.
Goodwife Petra: It is a hole with rainwater at the bottom. It makes a noise when the bucket hits.
Goodwife Petra: And a dog howls in the dark because it is cold and its master is in the ground. That is what dogs are for.
-> goodwife_menu

~ poison
Goodwife Petra: Nobody. That's the point. There's nothing left here worth the trouble. Only the water, and the walk to it, and being home before the light goes.
-> END

~ woodcutter
if quest.cut_after_noon and quest.cut_after_noon != rumored
-> village_of_barovia/cut_after_noon:grigore
endif
Grigore: Out of the road, out of the road. This load won't carry itself, and the light won't wait for it.
* Why the hurry? -> woodcutter_hurry
* [if flag.luca_rumor] We heard about your lad. -> village_of_barovia/cut_after_noon:asks
* Sorry. -> END

~ woodcutter_hurry
Grigore: The trees by the west road, you cut what you need by noon and you go. After noon they're not the same trees. Ask anyone who stayed to cut a bit more.
Grigore: Nobody? No. That's my point.
* Somebody stayed, didn't they? -> village_of_barovia/cut_after_noon:asks
* We'll let you get on. -> END

~ widow
if quest.polite_caller and quest.polite_caller != rumored
-> village_of_barovia/polite_caller:day
endif
if flag.burgomaster_buried
Widow Ileana: The burgomaster has a proper grave now, over there. My Teodor will be glad of the company. He never liked him, mind.
-> widow_menu
endif
Widow Ileana: I'm telling him the news. There's never any news. He doesn't mind; he was always a good listener, and now he's a better one.
-> widow_menu

~ widow_menu
* Who was he? -> widow_who
* [if flag.teodor_rumor or flag.teodor_grave_known] They say you leave your shutter open at night. -> village_of_barovia/polite_caller:asks
* We'll leave you to it. -> END

~ widow_who
Widow Ileana: Teodor. A cooper. He went to fetch a barrel from the crossroads one evening and came back the next morning, quite well, only very pale and very polite. Father Donavich made me shut the door on him.
Widow Ileana: I did. I still don't know if I was right.
* Has he come back since? -> village_of_barovia/polite_caller:asks
* We're sorry. -> END

~ gravedigger
if flag.ilarion_home
Old Mihail: My father's home. He's younger than I was when I dug his grave. I filled it in this morning and stood on it, and I don't know what I felt. Petra says that's allowed.
-> END
endif
if flag.bride_buried
Old Mihail: No grave this week. I keep picking up the spade and putting it down again. Petra says I'm to dig her a herb bed instead. Herbs don't need six feet.
-> END
endif
Old Mihail: Mind the edge. It's deeper than it looks. They all are, now. Six feet was enough once. Six feet isn't enough any more.
* Who is it for? -> gravedigger_who
* Why so deep? -> gravedigger_deep
* [if flag.sixfeet_rumor and (not quest.six_feet or quest.six_feet == rumored)] Arik says you dig your graves early. -> village_of_barovia/six_feet:asks
* [if (flag.teodor_rumor or quest.polite_caller) and not flag.teodor_grave_known] Did you ever dig a grave for Teodor the cooper? -> gravedigger_teodor
* [if level >= 3 and not quest.the_nursemaids_grave] Anyone you couldn't bury? -> village_of_barovia/the_nursemaids_grave:mihail
* Goodbye. -> END

~ gravedigger_who
Old Mihail: Nobody yet. There's always somebody by the end of the week. I like to be ready. It's rude to keep them waiting.
* [if not quest.six_feet or quest.six_feet == rumored] How do you know there'll be somebody? -> village_of_barovia/six_feet:asks
* Goodbye. -> END

~ gravedigger_deep
Old Mihail: So they stay down. Some of them try to come home, see. Not the ones I've buried. Not yet. I dig deep and I pack it hard.
-> END

~ gravedigger_teodor
set teodor_grave_known
if not quest.polite_caller
quest polite_caller rumored
endif
Old Mihail: Teodor Cozma. I dug for him three winters back, the week he went to the crossroads. Good and deep. Nobody ever came to fill it.
Old Mihail: It's by the east wall, still open. I keep the rain out of it. It seemed rude not to.
Old Mihail: Somebody's been putting things in it, mind. Of a night. I don't look. A grave's a private place.
-> END

~ acolyte
if flag.anca_letters
Anca [smile]: Good morning. Look, on the broom handle: I scratched my letters into the ash-wood with a nail.
Anca: Even if the rain washes the path clean, the broom remembers.
else
Anca: Good morning. Father Donavich says a swept path is a prayer you can walk on. I sweep it twice, to be sure.
endif
if flag.burgomaster_buried
Anca: It's quieter under the floor since the burial. I sleep better. Father doesn't.
endif
-> acolyte_menu

~ acolyte_menu
* [if not flag.burgomaster_buried] What's under the floor? -> acolyte_floor
* [if not flag.anca_letters] Can you read? -> anca_ask
* [if flag.anca_letters and not flag.anca_secret_known] [Insight DC 12] (She hums at the cellar grate as she sweeps. It isn't a hymn.) -> anca_secret_notice | anca_secret_miss
* Goodbye. -> END

~ acolyte_floor
Anca: Nothing. The cellar. Father says it's the wind in the cellar. The wind says his name, sometimes, and asks for him.
Anca: I sweep a bit louder when it does.
-> acolyte_menu

~ anca_ask
Anca: Read? No. Nobody here has the ink to waste on girls.
Anca [weary]: Father Donavich says a swept path is a prayer, and the Morninglord hears broom-straw as clearly as a hymn.
Anca: Still. I'd like to know what the big book by the altar says about the people we put in the ground.
* (Write her name in the dirt with a stick.) -> anca_teach
* Not now. -> acolyte_menu

~ anca_teach
set anca_letters
Narrator: You take a dry twig from the ditch and scratch four letters into the grey dirt by her boots.
Anca: That first one looks like a church roof with a beam across to hold the snow up.
Narrator: She takes the stick from your hand, her knuckles chapped red from the morning cold, and traces the groove.
Anca: And the last one is the same roof again. That seems thrifty. I can remember thrifty.
Narrator: She scratches all four letters beside yours, smaller and crooked, then stands back to look.
Anca [smile]: There. Now the path knows who sweeps it.
approve liriel_dawnsong +1 godrick_pendlebrook +1: You taught Anca to write her name
-> acolyte_menu

~ anca_secret_notice
Narrator: When the broom passes the cellar grate, she hums three low notes that belong to no hymn you have heard.
Anca [afraid]: That's only the boards settling. Old wood makes all sorts of noises when the damp gets in.
* You can tell us. -> anca_secret
* We won't pry. -> acolyte_menu

~ anca_secret_miss
Narrator: You watch her face for some small twitch of guilt or memory, but she only sweeps the same grey flagstone a third time.
-> acolyte_menu

~ anca_secret
set anca_secret_known
Anca [sad]: Please don't look at the grate like that. It makes him quiet, and the quiet is worse for him.
Anca: I only tell him the weather when I sweep. Nobody has told him anything since Father locked the padlock.
Anca: Most days I tell him the mist is down to the well-head and the crows are on the lychgate.
Anca [sad]: Today I told him the sun came out over the woods. It's a small lie, and the floorboards are thick.
Anca [afraid]: Don't tell Father Donavich. He prays so loud to drown the cellar out, and his knees are already raw.
approve liriel_dawnsong +1 thistle +1: You kept Anca's secret
-> acolyte_menu

~ vasile
Vasile: You heard about the burgomaster? Dead. Heart gave out. The wolves stood round the house all night like mourners.
Petre: It wasn't his heart.
Vasile: It was his heart, Petre. Something took it.
-> vasile_menu

~ vasile_menu
* Heard anything interesting? -> gossip
* [if not quest.the_fourth_rumour] Ever thought of having a fourth rumour? -> fourth_rumour
* [if quest.the_fourth_rumour == offered] About that fourth rumour. -> village_of_barovia/the_fourth_rumour:seeds
* [if flag.fourth_rumour_echoed and quest.the_fourth_rumour == planted] About that rumour of ours. -> village_of_barovia/the_fourth_rumour:thanks
* Goodbye. -> END

# The Fourth Rumour starts here, so Vasile and Petre's own conversation file moves it (tests/integration/test_side_quest_reach.gd).
~ fourth_rumour
if not quest.the_fourth_rumour
quest the_fourth_rumour offered
endif
-> village_of_barovia/the_fourth_rumour:offer

~ petre
Petre: Strangers. Haven't had strangers since the last strangers. They didn't stay long either. Nobody does, except us.
Vasile: We'd leave if we could. Road's open. You just come back round to the gate.
Petre: In the mist. Every time.
-> petre_menu

~ petre_menu
* Heard anything interesting? -> gossip
* That's a good coat. -> petre_coat
* [if not quest.the_fourth_rumour] Ever thought of having a fourth rumour? -> fourth_rumour
* [if quest.the_fourth_rumour == offered] About that fourth rumour. -> village_of_barovia/the_fourth_rumour:seeds
* [if flag.fourth_rumour_echoed and quest.the_fourth_rumour == planted] About that rumour of ours. -> village_of_barovia/the_fourth_rumour:thanks
* Goodbye. -> END

~ petre_coat
if flag.petre_coat_known
Petre: It's still a good coat. We've said all there is to say about it.
-> petre_menu
endif
Petre: It keeps the wet off my shoulders. That's all a coat needs to do in this place.
Petre [weary]: Never mind the stitching. Ask a man about the weather if you want to make small talk.
* [Persuasion DC 11] It's a good coat. You wear it like a good memory. -> petre_coat_told | petre_coat_shut
* [if gold >= 1] (Press a gold piece into his hand.) -> petre_coat_paid
* Another time. -> petre_menu

~ petre_coat_shut
Petre [weary]: Draft's coming straight through the boards tonight. Going to rain before morning, if the fog lets it.
-> petre_menu

~ petre_coat_paid
gold -1
Narrator: Petre catches the coin in both chapped hands and slips it deep into his lining as though it might go off.
Petre [afraid]: Put that away before someone sees it shine. Gold has a bad habit of outliving the pockets it sits in.
Petre [weary]: Still. That's firewood through the new moon, and salt besides. May the mist leave your road clear.
Petre [weary]: You keep staring at the wool. Suppose a whole gold piece buys you the right to stare.
Petre: Better you hear it from me than get the wrong idea in the tavern.
Petre: All right. The coat.
-> petre_coat_told

~ petre_coat_told
set petre_coat_known
Petre [sad]: It was the burgomaster's daughter. Ireena. The first hard frost after my roof gave in, I had only a sack over my shirt.
Petre: She came down the steps with it over her arm and said it was too broad in the shoulder for her brother.
Petre [sad]: A grown man ought not be cold enough to take good wool from a girl's hands. Still, the wind was off the mountain.
Petre: She never looks at it when she passes me in the street. That is the best part of the charity.
Petre [weary]: Keep it to yourself, mind. If Vasile hears, he'll be coughing under her window before dark.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +1 liriel_dawnsong +1: Petre told you where the coat came from
-> petre_menu

# "Heard anything interesting?" (docs/story/side_quests.md): the same three rumours, in turns, and how they ended. Asked
# again with nothing to add, they say so (batch 1 of the NPC plan): three ways, and one rumour that is wrong.
~ gossip
set gossip_spoke = 0
if not flag.gossip_asked
Vasile: Interesting? In Barovia? We've had the same three rumours since the mist came down. We take turns.
endif
if not quest.polite_caller
set gossip_spoke += 1
set teodor_rumor
quest polite_caller rumored
Vasile: Widow Ileana leaves her shutter open a crack every night. Says it's for the smoke.
Petre: It's not for the smoke.
Vasile: I know it's not for the smoke, Petre. That's what makes it a rumour.
elif flag.teodor_fate == "dawn" and not flag.gossip_told_teodor
set gossip_spoke += 1
set gossip_told_teodor
Petre: Widow Ileana shuts her shutter at night now. Sleeps, too, she says. First time in three winters.
elif flag.teodor_fate == "woods" and not flag.gossip_told_teodor
set gossip_spoke += 1
set gossip_told_teodor
Petre: Widow Ileana still leaves her shutter open. Says she sleeps better. Two knocks, now and then, from the woods side.
elif flag.teodor_fate == "ended" and not flag.gossip_told_teodor
set gossip_spoke += 1
set gossip_told_teodor
Vasile: Widow Ileana's put garlic up. First time ever. She doesn't talk to anyone now.
endif
if not quest.cut_after_noon
set gossip_spoke += 1
set luca_rumor
quest cut_after_noon rumored
Petre: Grigore's lad, Luca. Went out for the last load two days back and came home after dark with it. Said nothing. Went to bed. Hasn't got up.
Vasile: Cut after noon, that's what. You don't cut after noon. Everybody knows you don't cut after noon.
Petre: Everybody but Luca.
elif flag.luca_awake and not flag.gossip_told_luca
set gossip_spoke += 1
set gossip_told_luca
Vasile: Grigore's lad is up and about. Won't go near the west road after dinner, though. Won't even look at it.
endif
if not quest.last_muster and quest.polite_caller and quest.cut_after_noon
set gossip_spoke += 1
set muster_rumor
quest last_muster rumored
Petre: And the riders. Every night, out at the gates, after midnight. Bones on horses.
Vasile: You can hear them from the east road if the wind's right. Lances knocking. Somebody giving orders.
Petre: Nobody goes to see. That's the one rumour we don't take turns on.
elif flag.bone_marshal_beaten and not flag.gossip_told_muster
set gossip_spoke += 1
set gossip_told_muster
Vasile: No riders at the gates any more. The wind's quiet. I don't like it.
Petre: You didn't like the riders.
Vasile: I knew where I was with the riders.
endif
if flag.children_rescued and flag.morgantha_slain and not quest.the_fourth_sister
set gossip_spoke += 1
quest the_fourth_sister rumored
Petre: The Sarnov woman walks up the miller's lane every morning now. Comes back with one plain pastry.
Vasile: From a girl who sells them up there. She says the girl's got her husband's eyes.
Petre: Her husband had the ordinary kind.
Vasile: That's what makes it a rumour, Petre.
elif flag.mouse_fate == "home" and not flag.gossip_told_sarnov
set gossip_spoke += 1
set gossip_told_sarnov
Petre: The Sarnovs have got three children again. Nobody's asking how.
Vasile: I'm asking.
Petre: You're not asking her, though.
endif
if not flag.burgomaster_buried and not flag.gossip_told_heart
set gossip_spoke += 1
set gossip_told_heart
Vasile: And the burgomaster. Heart.
Petre: Wasn't his heart.
elif flag.burgomaster_buried and not flag.gossip_told_burial
set gossip_spoke += 1
set gossip_told_burial
if flag.burial_method == "church_rites"
Petre: And they buried the burgomaster. Properly, with the priest.
Vasile: Took them long enough. He was starting to be a rumour himself.
elif flag.burial_method == "cleric_rites"
Petre: And they buried the burgomaster. Properly, too. One of the strangers said the prayers over him.
Vasile: Took them long enough. He was starting to be a rumour himself.
else
Petre: And they buried the burgomaster. No priest, mind.
Vasile: Took them long enough. He was starting to be a rumour himself.
endif
endif
set gossip_asked
if flag.gossip_spoke == 0
-> gossip_nothing
endif
-> END

# Nothing new to say (owner's "not everything should give us information", 2026-10-17): in turn, the second time is the
# wrong rumour, which Goodwife Petra puts right.
~ gossip_nothing
set gossip_nothing += 1
if flag.gossip_nothing == 1
Vasile [angry]: Again? You asked us that an hour ago. Do we look like men to whom things happen on the hour?
Petre: A crow sat on the well-beam. Then it flew off toward the woods. That was the afternoon.
Vasile [weary]: It was the same crow as this morning. I know its bad foot.
Petre: There you are, then. Come back at dusk if you want to hear about the mud.
elif flag.gossip_nothing == 2
set vasile_wrong_heard
Vasile [sly]: If you must know, the late burgomaster's old wolfhound has begun to speak. Plain as you or me, just after midnight.
Petre: It has not.
Vasile: One single word, every night, right at the kennel fence. Enough to chill the marrow in your shins.
Petre [weary]: Go on, then. What word does it say, Vasile?
Vasile: It says "Woof." But with a terrible, knowing weight to it.
elif flag.gossip_nothing == 3
Vasile: Well, Old Mihail's spade broke in the frost, if you missed that the first four times.
Petre: That was last month, Vasile. You cannot keep serving last month to guests.
Vasile [sly]: They're from out of the valley. Last month is brand new to them.
Petre [weary]: Pay him no mind. Nobody has died since breakfast, and we are all very put out about it.
else
Vasile: Three whole days without a screaming in the lane. That has to be a record since the fog came.
Petre [afraid]: Don't say it out loud, you fool. The quiet only means it's taking a breath.
Vasile [weary]: Let it breathe, then. My knees ache less when nothing is chasing us.
endif
-> END

~ goat
Narrator: The goat looks up from the fence it is eating, considers you, and goes back to the fence. It has seen worse than you, and it has eaten better fences.
* [if spell:speak_with_animals] Ask the goat what it's seen. -> goat_speaks
* [if not spell:speak_with_animals] [knows:speak_with_animals] (Cast Speak with Animals, and ask the goat what it's seen.) -> goat_cast
* [if spell:speak_with_animals or knows:speak_with_animals] Leave it to the fence. -> END
-> END

~ goat_cast
cast speak_with_animals
if check.last
-> goat_speaks
endif
-> END

# Speak with Animals (2024 PHB): the goat has tasted most of the village, including the barn's stash.
~ goat_speaks
Narrator: The goat answers with its mouth full, and doesn't stop chewing to do it.
Narrator: "The old barn that fell down. Under the beams there's a long stick with a sharp shiny head, wrapped up in sacking. Tastes of storms. I spat it out."
reveal barn_beams_stash
Narrator: "And the god-house screams every night, when the sun goes. Don't eat anything near the god-house."
-> END

# The goat in places it cannot be (NPC plan batch 1, the first three of its sightings; the rest come with the later
# regions): Bildrath's shop, the church nave, the Death House gate. Speak with Animals gets a word from it each time.
~ goat_shop
Narrator: The village goat is standing between two barrels of salt pork, methodically eating a paper price tag off a coil of hemp rope.
Narrator: Bildrath is looking over its head at the door, as if a goat in his shop is a matter between the goat and the inventory.
Narrator: The corner of the tag still showing says thirty silver pieces. The goat swallows it without blinking.
* [if spell:speak_with_animals] Ask the goat what it thinks of the shop. -> goat_shop_speaks
* [if not spell:speak_with_animals] [knows:speak_with_animals] (Cast Speak with Animals, and ask the goat what it thinks of the shop.) -> goat_shop_cast
* Leave it to its dinner. -> END

~ goat_shop_cast
cast speak_with_animals
if check.last
-> goat_shop_speaks
endif
-> END

~ goat_shop_speaks
Narrator: The goat chews twice before answering you. Its voice is flat, patient, and slightly muffled by twine.
Narrator: "Tastes of Bildrath's thumb," it says. "Which is to say it tastes of tallow and nothing at all, only very dear."
Narrator: "The ink is the best part. He buys the good ink to write the bad numbers."
-> END

~ goat_church
Narrator: The goat is standing on the third pew from the front, all four hooves planted neatly on the kneeler.
Narrator: It is eating the corner of a hymn-book page with slow, even pulls. Goodwife Sorina has turned her shawl to face the wall.
Narrator: When the page comes free, the goat does not hurry to the next one. It has all afternoon.
* [if spell:speak_with_animals] Ask the goat what it makes of the church. -> goat_church_speaks
* [if not spell:speak_with_animals] [knows:speak_with_animals] (Cast Speak with Animals, and ask the goat what it makes of the church.) -> goat_church_cast
* Leave it to its hymn. -> END

~ goat_church_cast
cast speak_with_animals
if check.last
-> goat_church_speaks
endif
-> END

~ goat_church_speaks
Narrator: The goat speaks around a mouthful of morning prayers. It sounds like an old parishioner who only comes for the roof.
Narrator: "The paper here is sweet from the damp," it says. "The priest's turnips out back are sweeter, when he remembers to plant them."
Narrator: "There is something hungry under the floorboards. I have decided it is none of my business."
-> END

~ goat_gate
Narrator: The goat is standing by the iron gate of the old house at the end of the lane, looking up at the dark windows.
Narrator: The upper windows look back down at the goat with the flat, patient attention of a house that does not like company.
Narrator: The goat chews a splinter from the gatepost and seems to have seen worse stonework.
* [if spell:speak_with_animals] Ask the goat about the house. -> goat_gate_speaks
* [if not spell:speak_with_animals] [knows:speak_with_animals] (Cast Speak with Animals, and ask the goat about the house.) -> goat_gate_cast
* Leave it to its splinter. -> END

~ goat_gate_cast
cast speak_with_animals
if check.last
-> goat_gate_speaks
endif
-> END

~ goat_gate_speaks
Narrator: The goat does not take its eyes off the third-floor window when it answers you.
Narrator: "Good dock-weed in the yard," it says. "Very rich soil. I do not ask why."
Narrator: "The little doll in the attic wants someone to come up and play. I prefer the fence."
-> END
